<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia sees 1996/97 citrus output down five pct.</title>
<headline>Tunisia sees 1996/97 citrus output down five pct.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia's output of citrus fruits in the 1996/1997 season (October-March) is put at 211,000 tonnes, including 101,000 tonnes of the &quot;maltese&quot; orange variety, agriculture minister Mabrouk Bahri said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Output was down five percent from 221,000 tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Exports of citrus, which started on January 11, totalled 11,722 tonnes to date worth 9.0 million dinars, Bahri told journalists.</p>
<p>Citrus exports totalled 25,000 tonnes last season.</p>
<p>France is Tunisia's traditional market for citrus. ($=1.08 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom +2161-787538</p>
</text>
